# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0
#
# Declarative structural assertions for the GTS transport slice — the
# slice-resident test-DSL twin of the MUST / MUST-NOT invariants formerly
# hand-written in tests/test_gts_slice.py. Authored as gmeow: ontology data so
# the same annotation discipline and the native Rust harness (crates/slicetest,
# #784) drive the test, not ad-hoc Python. Each assertion runs as a SPARQL ASK
# over the slice module graph (gmeow:scopeModule).
#
# FAITHFULNESS NOTES:
#  * The artifact-spine cell (saArtifactClassesGroundInSpine) asserts subClassOf
#    edges whose PARENT classes (gmeow:Manifestation / gmeow:Activity /
#    gmeow:InformationObject) live in OTHER slices — but the subClassOf TRIPLE's
#    home is gts/module.ttl, so a scopeModule ASK sees it. (Contrast temporal's
#    cross-slice must-stays, where the SUBJECT itself is absent.)
#  * The two dynamic universals (saEveryCodecCarriesACodecClass,
#    saSliceTermsAreClassOrPropertyTyped) are MUST-NOT ASKs with FILTER NOT
#    EXISTS over a TYPE pattern — NOT a hand-listed VALUES blacklist — so a future
#    codec or term added without the required typing trips them.
#  * saOpacityReasonExactClosedSet re-expresses the pytest's `== {3 reasons}`
#    closed equality as a MUST-NOT `FILTER ?r NOT IN (the 3)`; faithful because
#    the pytest itself fixed the set to exactly those three (NOT a dynamic
#    universal weakened to a blacklist).
#
# TWO pytest fns stay in tests/test_gts_slice.py:
#  * test_value_vocabulary_cardinality_floors — the numeric cardinality (>=7
#    GTSProfile, >=7 TransformCodec, ==3 CodecClass): a boolean ASK cannot assert
#    a count. The NAMED individuals + the OpacityReason exact set ARE migrated
#    below; only the count floors remain.
#  * test_competency_queries_parse_and_run — a parse+execute SMOKE over
#    queries/*.rq with NO pinned expected result; a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion cell
#    REQUIRES an expected outcome, so authoring one would fabricate an assertion
#    the pytest never made.
#
# See dsl/tests/MIGRATION-LEDGER.md for the per-test pytest→DSL mapping.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/gts/tests/> .

# --- 1. Artifact classes ground in the existing spine (MUST) -----------------
ex:saArtifactClassesGroundInSpine a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:GTSDocument   rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:Manifestation .
    gmeow:GTSSegment    rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:Manifestation .
    gmeow:GTSCompaction rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:Activity .
    gmeow:OpaqueFrame   rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:InformationObject .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "GTS artifact classes MUST ground in the existing spine: gmeow:GTSDocument / gmeow:GTSSegment ⊑ gmeow:Manifestation, gmeow:GTSCompaction ⊑ gmeow:Activity, gmeow:OpaqueFrame ⊑ gmeow:InformationObject (the subClassOf triples are home-asserted in gts/module.ttl even though the parents live in other slices). Mirrors test_artifact_classes_ground_in_existing_spine." .

# --- 2. gtsHeadId is a version fingerprint (MUST) ----------------------------
ex:saHeadIdIsVersionFingerprint a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK { gmeow:gtsHeadId rdfs:subPropertyOf gmeow:versionFingerprint . }""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The chain head transitively commits to history — a fingerprint, not a byte digest: gmeow:gtsHeadId MUST be a subPropertyOf gmeow:versionFingerprint (the no-parallel-mechanisms seam). Mirrors test_head_id_is_a_version_fingerprint." .

# --- 3. Structure properties are part-of the spine (MUST) --------------------
ex:saStructurePropertiesArePartOfSpine a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:gtsSegmentOf rdfs:subPropertyOf gmeow:partOf .
    gmeow:opaqueFrameIn rdfs:subPropertyOf gmeow:partOf .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Segment-of and frame-in walk as partOf so disclosure coarsening (P10 generalizesVia default) traverses transport containment: gmeow:gtsSegmentOf / gmeow:opaqueFrameIn MUST each be a subPropertyOf gmeow:partOf. Mirrors test_structure_properties_are_part_of_spine." .

# --- 4. No parallel signature or digest mechanism (MUST-NOT) -----------------
ex:saNoParallelSignatureOrDigest a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    VALUES ?t { gmeow:gtsSignature gmeow:gtsDigest gmeow:gtsContentDigest }
    { ?t ?p ?o . } UNION { ?s ?t ?o . } UNION { ?s ?p ?t . }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The slice MUST reuse attestation/sources, never mint its own signature or byte-digest terms: none of gmeow:gtsSignature / gmeow:gtsDigest / gmeow:gtsContentDigest MUST appear in ANY triple position (a FIXED forbidden set, exactly as the pytest hardcodes). Mirrors test_no_parallel_signature_or_digest_mechanism." .

# --- 5. Every codec carries a codecClass (MUST-NOT, DYNAMIC) -----------------
ex:saEveryCodecCarriesACodecClass a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    ?c a gmeow:TransformCodec .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?c gmeow:codecClass ?cc }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Every gmeow:TransformCodec MUST carry a gmeow:codecClass — a DYNAMIC universal (FILTER NOT EXISTS over the type pattern, NOT a hand-listed codec set), so a future codec added without a class trips it. NOTE: scopeModule-narrowed vs the pytest's merged-graph scan — faithful for slice-owned codecs; other slices' codecs are out of the harness's reach BY CONSTRUCTION (the same accepted narrowing as the artifact-spine cell), not a scope bug. Mirrors test_every_codec_carries_a_codec_class." .

# --- 6. Every slice term is class- or property-typed (MUST-NOT, DYNAMIC) ------
ex:saSliceTermsAreClassOrPropertyTyped a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    ?s ?p ?o .
    FILTER( isIRI(?s) && STRSTARTS(STR(?s), "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/") )
    FILTER( STR(?s) != "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts" )
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
        ?s a ?owltype .
        FILTER( ?owltype IN (owl:Class, owl:ObjectProperty, owl:DatatypeProperty, owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:Ontology) )
    }
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
        ?s a ?gtype .
        FILTER( isIRI(?gtype) && STRSTARTS(STR(?gtype), "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/") )
    }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Every gmeow-namespaced subject in the module (except the slice ontology IRI) MUST be properly typed — either OWL-declared (owl:Class/ObjectProperty/DatatypeProperty/FunctionalProperty/Ontology) or a gmeow:-typed individual. A DYNAMIC sweep (FILTER NOT EXISTS over both typing patterns, mirroring the pytest's `allowed` set + individual escape), NOT a hand-listed term blacklist. Mirrors test_slice_terms_are_class_or_property_typed." .

# --- 7. Named value-vocabulary individuals are seeded (MUST) ------------------
ex:saValueVocabNamedIndividualsSeeded a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    gmeow:gtsProfileDist      a gmeow:GTSProfile .
    gmeow:gtsProfileEvidence  a gmeow:GTSProfile .
    gmeow:gtsProfileAiPackage a gmeow:GTSProfile .
    gmeow:codecZstd           a gmeow:TransformCodec .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Open value vocabularies (P9): the named individuals gmeow:gtsProfileDist / gmeow:gtsProfileEvidence / gmeow:gtsProfileAiPackage MUST be typed gmeow:GTSProfile and gmeow:codecZstd MUST be typed gmeow:TransformCodec. Mirrors the named-individual clauses of test_value_vocabularies_are_seeded (the >=7 / ==3 cardinality floors stay in pytest)." .

# --- 8. The three OpacityReason individuals are seeded (MUST) -----------------
ex:saOpacityReasonIndividualsSeeded a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    gmeow:opacityUnknownCodec a gmeow:OpacityReason .
    gmeow:opacityMissingKey   a gmeow:OpacityReason .
    gmeow:opacityDamaged      a gmeow:OpacityReason .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The three reality-monitoring opacity reasons MUST be individuals of gmeow:OpacityReason. Mirrors the OpacityReason existence clause of test_value_vocabularies_are_seeded." .

# --- 9. OpacityReason is an EXACT closed set of three (MUST-NOT) --------------
ex:saOpacityReasonExactClosedSet a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    ?r a gmeow:OpacityReason .
    FILTER( ?r NOT IN ( gmeow:opacityUnknownCodec, gmeow:opacityMissingKey, gmeow:opacityDamaged ) )
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:OpacityReason is a CLOSED set of exactly three: NO gmeow:OpacityReason individual MUST exist outside {opacityUnknownCodec, opacityMissingKey, opacityDamaged}. This re-expresses the pytest's `== {3}` closed equality (NOT a Gap-1 weakening — the pytest itself fixed the set). Mirrors the OpacityReason exact-set clause of test_value_vocabularies_are_seeded." .
